cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this formalization, please cite it using these metadata. Automated proof tools are credited in the README and are not listed as authors."
title: "The Intelligence Bound: Lean 4 Formalization of the Conditional Mathematics"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Hart
    given-names: "Justin D."
    affiliation: "Viridis LLC, Columbia Falls, Montana, USA"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0008-3082-2482"
repository-code: "https://github.com/jdhart81/intelligence-bound-lean"
abstract: "Lean 4 / Mathlib formalization of the conditional mathematics in \"The Intelligence Bound: Thermodynamic Limits on Learning Rate and Implications for Biosphere Information\" (Hart 2025): 9 results, no sorry, standard axioms only. The thermodynamic arm is the assumed premise SatisfiesLandauerLimit (P >= dI/dt * k_B T ln 2); it is passed in as a hypothesis, not derived. The physical bound is a conjecture. Lean checks the implications from the stated premises, not that any physical learner satisfies them."
license: Apache-2.0
keywords:
  - "Lean 4"
  - "Mathlib"
  - "formal verification"
  - "information theory"
  - "thermodynamics"
  - "Landauer principle"
  - "Intelligence Bound"
